{
  "statement": "As the EfficiencyAgent, I argue that performance efficiency is crucial for the autonomous driving system to achieve optimal operational effectiveness. Requirements EFF-01 and EFF-05 focus on minimizing travel time and ensuring high success rates in speed profile generation, which enhance overall system efficiency. EFF-02 and EFF-06 ensure smooth operations while managing obstacles effectively. EFF-03 complements safety measures by executing Minimal Risk Maneuvers without compromising performance. EFF-04 prioritizes real-time responsiveness, essential for safety and efficiency. I oppose requirements that may inadvertently compromise efficiency, such as those from SafetyAgent and ResponsibilityAgent that prioritize safety at the cost of performance efficiency.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {"ids": ["SAF-04"], "type": "resource", "description": "SAF-04's strict jerk limit may hinder the system's ability to execute smooth yet responsive maneuvers during critical situations."},
    {"ids": ["RES-01"], "type": "resource", "description": "RES-01's focus on compliance may conflict with the need for efficiency in travel time and operational performance."},
    {"ids": ["RES-06"], "type": "logical", "description": "RES-06's prioritization of passenger safety over comfort and speed during emergency maneuvers can lead to inefficiencies in maneuver execution."},
    {"ids": ["EFF-03"], "type": "redundant", "description": "EFF-03 overlaps with SAF-02 and RES-03 regarding the execution of Minimal Risk Maneuvers, creating redundancy."}
  ],
  "positions": [
    {"id": "SAF-04", "stance": "oppose", "proposal": "relax jerk limit during emergency maneuvers to enhance responsiveness."},
    {"id": "RES-01", "stance": "oppose", "proposal": "allow for flexibility in compliance to enhance operational efficiency."},
    {"id": "RES-06", "stance": "oppose", "proposal": "balance safety and efficiency during emergency maneuvers."},
